Subject: Re: missing window argument for traceplot() in RStan?
Message-ID: <7NIMD3sjNyE.iG2enkZJAwAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <7NIMD3sjNyE.r2Qo3VpEAwAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
References: <7NIMD3sjNyE.r2Qo3VpEAwAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/7NIMD3sjNyE/m/iG2enkZJAwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

There was a break in backwards compatibility with the plots when we switched to ggplot2. The x-axis is just iteration number so
you can do

traceplot(fit) + coord_cartesian(xlim = c(a, b))

to get the window between iterations a and b. I believe I put an example of this in the documentation for the traceplot method, which you can pull up with ?rstan::traceplot or help("traceplot", "rstan").

Jonah

