MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

For scaling other than unit scaling, Stan has to figure
out the scale during adaptation.

Non-centering (what we used to call the "Matt trick")
refers to *both* the mean and the log scale.  And it makes
an even bigger difference in multiple dimensions.

- Bob

> On Feb 19, 2016, at 7:24 AM, Sierra <sierra.ch...@gmail.com> wrote:
>
> If there are no suggestions to improve this sampling, does anyone have an intuition as to why one scaling would be harder for the sampler than the other?
>
> On Tuesday, February 16, 2016 at 11:19:17 AM UTC-5, Sierra wrote:
