For Responses : the model is Rasch model with parameters theta and betaR
logit(P) = theta - betaR

For Responses Times : the model is lognormal with parameter tau, betaT and sigmaT.
log(RT) ~ Normal(tau - betaT, sigmaT)

In 2nd level,
paramP is a vector (theta and tau) and paramI is vector (betaR and betaT).

So paramP ~ MultiNormal (muP,sigmaP) and paramI ~ MultiNormal(muI, sigmaI)

One suggestion I got was to rely on what has been done one page 75 of the manuel to write 2nd level.

Using script with my understanding, I write the model below

data {

   int P; // # Individus

   int Q; // # Items

   real logTwNA[P,Q]; // Log responses times

