> However, in your model definition the same betas are used for every component.

My mistake --- I meant "assuming betas is made into a matrix", but what
I should've said is array of vectors so we don't need an extra transpose
and it will work more efficiently by reference (see the manual chapter on
arrays vs. vectors):

  vector[M] betas[3];

Then X[n] is a row vector and beta[k] is a column vector, so
the product is a scalar.

- Bob

From u8c6a877154df740e at groups.google.com  Wed Mar  2 19:13:21 2016
