I might be missing something but I think you want to add to lp[k] instead of redefining it. Right now you set lp equal to log(theta) but then set it equal to something else when you set lp[k] to the result of normal_log(...). So I think you want lp[k] <- lp[k] + normal_log(...).

In generated quantities you should be able to do exactly the same thing you do in the model block but instead of incrementing the log probability you just want to save its value.

Jonah

