Hi Eric,

The NaN for the rhat for those elements of the cholesky are ok because a cholesky factor is a triangular matrix. Those elements aren't estimated.

Regarding the time it takes to fit the model there's no "normal". It will depend on how many parameters there are, the posterior geometry, the amount of data, how efficient your code is, etc.

Jonah

