From ub30c14c8b83478cb at groups.google.com  Fri Mar 11 19:31:16 2016
From: ub30c14c8b83478cb at groups.google.com (Gregory)
Date: Fri, 11 Mar 2016 19:31:16 +0000
Subject: Auto-regressive ordered logistic regression
Message-ID: <zC3UZJj71ek.M17eK-CaBgAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/zC3UZJj71ek/m/M17eK-CaBgAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello everyone,

I'm putting together an auto-regressive ordered logistic regression model, where the interpretation relates to the value of the latent variable yStar.

At the latent-variable level, the model is the following: yStar_t ~ logistic(beta * x1 + rho * yStar_{t -1}, 1)

At the observed-variable level: y_t ~ ordered_logistic(beta * x1 + rho * yStar_{t -1}, kappa)

I started with the simplest version of this model: a single cut point and a single covariate.

I set the model up in Stan in two steps:

(1) draws are made from the posterior for the values of yStar using a truncated logistic density: given the observed value of y, the latent variable yStar is known to be within a given range as defined by the cut point parameters

(2) ordered_logistic() is used to estimate the regression of interest for the observed variable

The problem is that I get the following error and I seem to have run out of ideas for where I'm going wrong:

[299] "  Log probability evaluates to log(0), i.e. negative infinity."
[300] "  Stan can't start sampling from this initial value."
[301] "Initialization between (--2, -2) failed after 100 attempts. "
[302] " Try specifying initial values, reducing ranges of constrained values, or reparameterizing the model."

Any suggestions for would great!

Simulation and model code:

library(rstan)

n_obs <- 2000
year <- 1:n_obs
x1 <- rnorm(n_obs, -1, 1) # Covariate

beta1 <- 0.4 # Parameter on covariate x1
rho <- 0.7 # Auto-regressive parameter

kappa <- c(-Inf, 0, Inf) # Cut points
k <- length(kappa) - 2 # Number of cut points

S <- data.frame(yStar = NA, y = NA, year = year, x1 = x1)

# Simulate first-order auto-regressive ordinal logistic regression data
for(t in 1:nrow(S)) {

  if(t == 1) { # Generate latent (linear) variable
    S$yStar[t] <- 0 # Arbitrary set yStar for t = 1
  } else {
    S$yStar[t] <- rho * S$yStar[t - 1] +
                  beta1 * x1[t] +
                  rlogis(1, 0, 1)
  }

  for(i in 1:(length(kappa) - 1)) { # Generate observed (ordered) variable
    if(S$yStar[t] > kappa[i] & S$yStar[t] <= kappa[i + 1]) S$y[t] <- i
  }

}

model_data <- list(n_obs = n_obs, y = S$y, year = S$year, x1 = S$x1)

model_code <- "
data {

  int n_obs;

  int y[n_obs];
  int year[n_obs];
  real x1[n_obs];

}

parameters {

  vector[n_obs] yStar; # Latent variable
  real rho; # Auto-regression parameter

  vector[1] beta; # Standard covariate parameters
  ordered[1] kappa; # Cut points

}

transformed parameters {
}

model {

  // Priors
  rho ~ normal(0, 5);

  beta ~ normal(0, 5);
  kappa ~ normal(0, 5);

  // Prior on first latent variable
  if(y[1] == 1) yStar[1] ~ normal(0, 5) T[, kappa[1]];
  if(y[1] == 2) yStar[1] ~ normal(0, 5) T[kappa[1], ];

  // Draws for yStar
  for(t in 2:n_obs) {

    if(y[t] == 1) {
      yStar[t] ~ logistic(rho * yStar[t - 1] +
                          beta[1] * x1[t],
                          1) T[, kappa[1]];
    }
    if(y[t] == 2) {
      yStar[t] ~ logistic(rho * yStar[t - 1] +
                          beta[1] * x1[t],
                          1) T[kappa[1], ];
    }
  }

  // Likelihood
  for(t in 2:n_obs) {
    y[t] ~ ordered_logistic(rho * yStar[t - 1] + beta[1] * x1[t], kappa);
  }
}

generated quantities {
}"

# Compile to C
model_latent <- stan_model(model_code = model_code)

# Sample from posterior
posterior_latent <- sampling(model_latent, data = model_data,
                             warmup = 1000, iter = 2000,
                             open_progress = FALSE, chains = 1)

