Hi Greg,

On Saturday, March 12, 2016 at 1:01:02 PM UTC-5, Gregory wrote:
> The constraint thus depends on the value(s) of kappa drawn at a given iteration. Can I do this in the transformed parameter or model block? Is there another way to do this?

kappa proposed, not kappa drawn

It can be done but you have to account for the change-of-variables and such models tend not to mix well.

parameters{
  pos_ordered[J - 1] kappa;
  vector<lower=0,upper=1>[N] u;
  real alpha;     // be sure to estimate this intercept since kappa is positive
  vector[K] beta;
}
model {
  vector[N] yStar;
  for (i in 1:N) {
    if (y[i] == 1) {
      yStar[i] <- u[i] * kappa[1];
      increment_log_prob(log(kappa[1]));
    }
    else if (y[i] < J) {
      real diff;
      diff <- kappa[y + 1] - kappa[y];
      yStar[i] <- u[i] * diff + kappa[y];
      increment_log_prob(log(diff));
    }
    else {
      yStar[i] <- kappa[J] / (1 - u[i]);
      increment_log_prob(log(kappa[j]) + 2 * log1m(u[i]));
    }
}

Ben

