On Thursday, March 17, 2016 at 7:38:14 AM UTC-4, Eric Innocents EBOULET wrote:
> I would like to modify sigmaP where I want to fix sigmaP[1] = 1 and to estimate L_SigmaP.
>
> parameters {
>
> vector[2] paramP[P]; // Parameters of persons (theta,tau)
>
> cholesky_factor_corr[2] L_OmegaP;
>
> vector<lower=0>[2] sigmaP;
>
>
> }

You cannot modify something declared in the parameters block. Instead, only declare a scalar standard deviation.

parameters {
  vector[2] paramP[P];

  cholesky_factor_corr[2] L_OmegaP;
  real<lower=0> sigmaP2;
}
model {
  matrix[2,2] L_SigmaP;
  vector[2] sigmaP;
  sigmaP[1] <- 1;

  sigmaP[2] <- sigmaP2;
  L_SigmaP <- diag_pre_multiply(sigmaP, L_OmegaP);

  ...
}

Ben

