On Saturday, March 12, 2016 at 12:08:20 PM UTC-5, Paul Buerkner wrote:
> Ok, I found out why the results differed. When I replicate the script of the OP exactly (including priors) I get the same  results as Ben.
>
> However, when I just call
>
> stanmod2 <- stan_glm(y~group-1, data=dat)
>
> I get some weired sigma estimates again. Also, the other parameters seem to be a bit off:

I believe this is due to the default priors of stan_glm being quite inconsistent with the data-generating process assumed by this model. If you nullify all the priors, you get something similar to the MLEs

stan_glm(y~group-1, data=dat, prior = NULL, prior_intercept = NULL, prior_ops = prior_options(scaled = FALSE))

Ben

