Subject: Implement a beta-possion in rstan
Message-ID: <z9FOYvI4fiI.aQejv8ttCAAJ@stan-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/stan-users/c/z9FOYvI4fiI/m/aQejv8ttCAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello,

I am a first time user of rstan. I implemented the following model using rstan, and got sampling results.
The implementation is so easy that I suspect its correctness.....
Could anyone read my code and give me some pointers?
Thanks in advance!

Jinrui

The model:
x|s,p ~ Poisson(s*p)
p|kon,koff ~ Beta(kon,koff)

hyper-priors
koff ~ Gamma(akoff, bkoff)
kon ~ Gamma(akon, bkon)
s ~ Gamma(as,bs)

My code:

dat <- read.table(fin)

x <- dat; x <- as.vector(x); x <- as.numeric(x);

x <- round(x,digits=0)

dataList <- list(

         N = length(x),

         x = as.vector(x),

         as = 1, bs = 0.001,

         akon = 1, bkon = 0.001,

         akoff = 1, bkoff = 0.001

         )

excode <- '

data {

  int<lower=0> N;  # number of cells

  int<lower=0> x[N]; # expression

  real<lower=0> as; # expression

  real<lower=0> bs; # expression

  real<lower=0> akon; # expression

  real<lower=0> bkon; # expression

  real<lower=0> akoff; # expression

  real<lower=0> bkoff; # expression

#  real spj[N];

}

parameters {

  real<lower=1e-100> s;

  real<lower=1e-100> kon;

  real<lower=1e-100> koff;

  real<lower=1e-100,upper=1> pj[N];

#  vector[N] mu;

#  vector[N] delta;

#  real delta_new;

}

transformed parameters {

  real spj[N];

  for (j in 1:N){

    spj[j] <- s*pj[j];

  }

}

model {

  kon ~ gamma(akon, bkon);

  koff ~ gamma(akoff, bkoff);

  s ~ gamma(as,bs);

  for( i in 1:N){

    pj[i] ~ beta(kon, koff);

    x[i] ~ poisson(spj[i]);

  }

}

'

